Why is this important?
Imagine five DevOps engineers are working on the same AWS infrastructure.

If each engineer maintains a separate local state file, they may have inconsistent information about the infrastructure.

Terraform remote state helps teams maintain a shared state file.

For example:
             DEVOPS TEAM
                  |
        ---------------------
        |         |         |
      User 1    User 2    User 3
        |         |         |
        ---------------------
                  |
              TERRAFORM
                  |
             AWS PROVIDER
                  |
             AWS RESOURCES
                  |
              S3 BACKEND
            (terraform.tfstate)


